            <ArticleTitle>Type-A coronary-prone behaviour.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>257-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The aetiology of coronary heart disease is still uncertain, and the standard risk factors have limited power to predict who will succumb to the disease. The hypothesis that psychological factors play a part has received fresh impetus with the results of research into type-A behaviour.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
